# ============================================================
# Line-ending contract (B5-01K)
# ============================================================
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so files are
# rewritten to CRLF on checkout unless told otherwise. That is fine for source,
# and NOT fine for files whose consumers parse them on Linux.
#
# `.nvmrc` is read by nvm/fnm/Volta locally, by actions/setup-node in CI
# (node-version-file), and by Render at deploy time — the last two on Linux. A
# CRLF checkout hands them "24.20.0\r" and they try to install a version with a
# trailing carriage return.
#
# This is not hypothetical. B5-01H shipped `#!/usr/bin/env node` in
# scripts/run-tests.js, autocrlf rewrote it to CRLF, and the CR defeated the
# shebang strip — the import failed with a bare "SyntaxError: Invalid or
# unexpected token" naming the wrong file. It passed review only because the
# file was still LF on the machine that wrote it. Do not repeat that with the
# runtime pin.
.nvmrc text eol=lf
